<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42423" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sălūtĭfer</span></b> ,
			fĕra, fĕrum, adj.
		salus-fero (<b>poet.</b> for salubris),
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>health-bringing</i>, <i>healing</i>, <i>salubrious</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">totique salutifer orbi Cresce, puer, dicit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					2, 642</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anguis Urbi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 15, 744</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">15, 632: herbae animantibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. Achill. 1, 117</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					5, 1, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 21, 174</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">salutiferā potione pestem veneni
					exstinguere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 10, p. 251, 29</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Aug. in Psa. 118</span></i>, Serm. 26, 4: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Alcim. 4, 225</span></i>
			.</div>
